<p>Credit control keeps a customer who is months behind from running up more on account, and reminds everyone who owes you, without anyone
  having to watch every sale. Both are in <strong>Settings › Preferences › Credit control</strong>, and both are off until an owner turns them on.</p>

<h2>Putting accounts on hold</h2>
<p>Set <strong>Put an account on hold when an invoice is overdue by more than</strong> a number of days, say 30. From then on, a customer with
  an invoice that late is on hold:</p>
<ul>
  <li>The till won't put anything more on their account without an owner's or manager's approval PIN. The customer's name shows
    <strong>On hold</strong> at the till.</li>
  <li>Their quotes can't be confirmed as orders without the same approval.</li>
  <li>Their page in <strong>Customers</strong> says why: how much is late, and by how many days.</li>
  <li>An approval to sell anyway is recorded on the sale and in <strong>Activity</strong>, with what was overdue.</li>
</ul>
<p>Paying the late invoices takes the hold off by itself; there's nothing to undo. Cash, M-Pesa and card sales are never affected. Set it to
  <strong>0</strong> to never hold accounts.</p>

<h2>Lifting a hold for a while</h2>
<p>When a customer has agreed to pay (a cheque coming on Friday, a payment plan), an owner or manager can open the customer and use
  <strong>Lift the hold</strong> for 7, 14 or 30 days, with the reason. The customer's page shows who lifted it, until when and why. When the
  time runs out the hold comes back if the invoices are still late. <strong>Put it back on hold now</strong> ends the lift early.</p>

<h2>Monday reminders</h2>
<p>Choose <strong>Every Monday, remind customers with overdue invoices</strong>: by SMS, or on WhatsApp with their statement. At 9 in the
  morning every customer with an overdue invoice, a phone number, and who hasn't asked not to be texted, gets a reminder of what they owe.</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>By SMS:</strong> needs texting switched on (<strong>Settings › SMS</strong>). With the
    <%= link_to "customer portal", help_article_path("customer-portal"), class: "link" %> on, the text links to their page, where they
    can see their invoices and pay with M-Pesa. A customer gets at most one reminder a day, however many people press the button.</li>
  <li><strong>On WhatsApp:</strong> needs WhatsApp from HardPoint switched on in <strong>Settings › Features</strong>. The statement for the
    last three months goes with it.</li>
</ul>
<p>You can still remind one customer at any time with <strong>Text a reminder</strong> or the WhatsApp button on their page.</p>
